From 520ba7636a9fbd29a887da7c8f19c9cccd1f10a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antigravity Tear <belmante@antigravity.io>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:46:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] filesystem: PackedDevice reads the game from a compact pack
 (game.rdpk)

A compact pack holds the game's files deduplicated: every distinct run of
bytes is stored once and each file is a list of extents into that store
(tools/make_compact_pack.py in RaymanOriginsRecomp). The files read back
byte for byte as the originals, from a memory-mapped pack.

SetupVfs mounts it when the game folder has a game.rdpk with the RDPK magic,
and the host folder otherwise. The entry XEX check accepts the pack too.
